          "source": "CBSE SQP 2024-25",
          "question": "For any two events $A$ and $B$, if $P(\\bar{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}$, $P(\\bar{B}) = \\dfrac{2}{3}$ and $P(A \\cap B) = \\dfrac{1}{4}$, then $P(\\bar{A}|\\bar{B})$ equals:",
          "options": [
            "$\\dfrac{3}{8}$",
            "$\\dfrac{8}{9}$",
            "$\\dfrac{5}{8}$",
            "$\\dfrac{1}{4}$"
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(C) $\\dfrac{5}{8}$",
            "concept": "$P(\\bar{A} \\cap \\bar{B}) = P\\big((A \\cup B)'\\big) = 1 - P(A \\cup B)$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Find $P(A)$ and $P(B)$.",
                "math": "P(A) = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{2},\\quad P(B) = 1 - \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{3}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Addition rule.",
                "math": "P(A \\cup B) = \\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{1}{4} = \\dfrac{7}{12}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Use De Morgan's law.",
                "math": "P(\\bar{A} \\cap \\bar{B}) = 1 - \\dfrac{7}{12} = \\dfrac{5}{12}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Apply the conditional probability formula.",
                "math": "P(\\bar{A}|\\bar{B}) = \\dfrac{P(\\bar{A} \\cap \\bar{B})}{P(\\bar{B})} = \\dfrac{5/12}{2/3} = \\dfrac{5}{8}",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Pick the matching option.",
                "math": "\\text{Option (C)}"
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Writing $P(\\bar{A} \\cap \\bar{B}) = 1 - P(A \\cap B)$: it is $1 - P(A \\cup B)$."
          }
        },
